# CODEOWNERS — audiomax.ai
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THESE ARE REVIEW ROLES, NOT GITHUB ACCOUNTS.
#
# The names below are Studio Zero review agents, not usernames or teams. GitHub
# resolves an owner to a user, a team or an email address, and none of these
# resolve to any of those — so GitHub will not auto-assign from this file and
# will report the entries as invalid if branch protection is switched on with
# "require review from Code Owners".
#
# This file is therefore ADVISORY until real handles exist. It answers "who
# reviews a change here, and against which persona" — which is the question that
# actually gets asked, and which was previously answered only by reading
# CLAUDE.md and the roadmap side by side.
#
# TO MAKE IT ENFORCEABLE: replace each role with the `@handle` of the human or
# team that carries it, keeping the role name in the trailing comment so the
# reasoning survives the substitution.
#
# Personas live at C:\Users\Administrator\studio-zero\agents\<layer>\<name>.md
# and are invoked by spawning a subagent with the persona file as its system
# context. Reviewers get READ-ONLY tools — Jury Rule 4 is enforced by tool
# scope, not by instructions.
#
# AUTHORITY. CLAUDE.md owns the agent roster. The ROADMAP is the sole authority
# for which reviewer gates which PHASE — this file maps PATHS, which is a
# different question, and it must not be read as a phase assignment. Where a
# path and a phase disagree, the roadmap wins and this file is defective.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Jury owns the commit gate for everything. No path is exempt.
*                               Jury            # audit/jury.md


